     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Ravi added two odd numbers and always got an even number.\n\"Why?\" he asked his teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "even",
     "odd",
     "palindrome"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Even numbers end in 0, 2, 4, 6 or 8 and odd numbers end in 1, 3, 5, 7 or 9. The sum of two odd numbers is even and the sum of two evens is even. Odd plus even is odd.\nA palindrome number reads the same both ways, like 1221. The Kaprekar routine reverses digits and subtracts to get a pattern.\nNumber puzzles help us see why rules hold, not just that they hold."
    }
   },
